.TH PMUX-PANE-WRITE 1 "September 2026" "Prismattyc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmux-pane-write \- send intentional text to one live pane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmux pane-write
.I PANE
.RB ( --text " TEXT" " | " --stdin )
.RB [ --submit " auto|enter|none" ]
.RB [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write literal UTF-8 text to the exact numeric pane ID.
The operation checks the current child PID and writes only to that pane.
Sync-input does not copy the text to sibling panes.
The operation does not acquire, take over, or release a controller lease.
.PP
Use this command for direct collaboration in a live agent pane or for an
explicitly authorized shell command.
Use
.B pmux mail send
for stored messages with claim/commit tracking.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --text " TEXT"
Send literal text. Backslash escapes are not decoded.
.TP
.B --stdin
Read the body from standard input. Choose exactly one of --text or --stdin.
.TP
.BI --submit " MODE"
The default, auto, uses bracketed paste and the detected agent's submit
sequence. Supported families are Grok, Claude, Kiro, Codex, and Cursor.
An unknown foreground application is refused.
Enter mode appends CR. None mode adds no submit key and leaves input dirty.
.TP
.B --json
Print a structured result on standard output.
.SH LIMITS AND REFUSALS
Text must contain 1 to 65,504 UTF-8 bytes.
Tabs and newlines are allowed. Other control characters are rejected.
Use pmux send for raw control keys.
.PP
Another controller, unsubmitted text, input within 750 ms, or at least
8 KiB of output in three seconds causes a refusal.
Activity checks do not prove that an application is ready.
.SH RESULTS
A queued result means the PTY input queue accepted all bytes.
It does not mean the recipient accepted, read, or executed the text.
Byte counts include paste framing and submit bytes.
.PP
A partial result means some bytes were queued before a failure.
The result includes accepted and total byte counts.
Inspect the pane before continuing. Do not automatically replay a partial
write or a write whose reply was lost.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means all bytes were queued. Nonzero means an error or partial write.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a message to an agent:
.PP
.nf
pmux pane-write 15 --text 'Review the parser change.' --json
.fi
.PP
Run a command in an authorized shell pane and inspect its output:
.PP
.nf
pmux pane-write 15 --text 'seq 1 10000' --submit enter --json
pmux save-buffer 15 -
.fi
.PP
Read a multiline body from a file:
.PP
.nf
pmux pane-write 15 --stdin --json < request.txt
.fi
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The daemon must support the pane_write operation.
Older daemons reject it; the CLI does not fall back to raw writes.
Installing binaries does not replace an already running daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmux (1),
.BR pmuxd (1),
.BR pmux-mcp (1)
